{"diagnosis": "mem_valid is inverted on instruction/data launch, hanging fetch at max_addr=0x00000000 with TRAP no progress. Line 584 drives mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word (0 for normal fetch) while line 598 asserts mem_valid == !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word (1 for normal fetch). The missing `!` means normal fetches never start a bus transfer and prefetched-high-word fetches spuriously do, stalling compressed prefetch.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -582,7 +582,7 @@
 				0: begin
 					if (mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst || mem_do_rdata) begin
-						mem_valid <= mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
+						mem_valid <= !mem_la_use_prefetched_high_word;
 						mem_instr <= mem_do_prefetch || mem_do_rinst;
 						mem_wstrb <= 0;
 						mem_state <= 1;", "expected": "tohost: PASS (vs FAIL 0xdead) with fetch progress max_addr > 0x00000000 and no TRAP no progress"}

